Storage Format Dictates Scalability: When an event can be reduced to a binary state, never store strings, objects, or relational rows. A single bit is all you need.
Harness Bare-Metal Hardware Instructions: Valkey's BITCOUNT is not a software loop—it maps directly to CPU POPCNT, executing in single-digit nanoseconds.
Partition by Time Bounds: Partitioning keys by Year (habit:{userId}:{habitId}:{year}) keeps memory blocks uniformly small (46 bytes), making caching, backup, and TTL archiving trivial.
