This postmortem reinforces three fundamental distributed systems principles:
HTTP 304 is a double-edged sword for Single Page Applications: HTTP caching is invaluable for static assets, but pairing automatic background revalidation with 304 Not Modified on mutable business state is an easy way to accidentally destroy client-side state.
Request Coalescing (SingleFlight) requires Mutation Epochs: Deduplicating concurrent database reads is critical for survival, but without epoch invalidation, slow reads will inevitably overwrite fast writes.
Embrace Client-Side Truth for Critical Actions: Under unpredictable mobile network conditions, client applications should maintain an authoritative local ledger of confirmed mutations rather than being at the mercy of lagging replicas.
